A||||12||Joe4x4||ECM..stick to auto ?||||1||
Z||000000||Joe4x4||02-06-2001||01:29 PM||||ok.....here is what I need to know. I`m working on my 86-4cyl auto...the ECM went bad on me, I bought a 84-4cyl stick for parts<BR>I took out the ECM out of the 84 stick and put it in the 86 auto it ran funny.<P>I tried than to take the PROM out of the 86 auto and use the ECM out of the 84 stick. and know it runs but ideals at 1500??<BR>and power is not there?<P>Should I find a 86 auto ECM ???<P>------------------<BR>Fiero got fire<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/exp.gif">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/animated_cat.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mbramble||02-06-2001||01:47 PM||||Look in Ogre's Cave (link at bottom of this page), go to the ECM section and select the Misc. Notes topic.  Should find an answer in there...||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||02-06-2001||06:57 PM||||You need the correct chip for the year, engine and transmission. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||02-06-2001||07:03 PM||||Slight correction. You need the correct chip for the ECM with the correct tranny. You generally can't move a chip from one ECM type to another. The 84 doesn't use the same ECM as the 86. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||02-06-2001||11:34 PM||||What about using an auto ECM from an '85 in a stick '85?  Both V6s of course.||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||02-07-2001||12:26 AM||||If you look, the 85 L4 ECM part numbers are the same. It's not the ECM that makes it an auto or manual, it's the chip. For an automatic, the code is in the chip for the TCC. For the manual, the code enables the stall-saver and uses the TCC output for the shift light. The calibrations are somewhat different to account for the way the trans act.<P>Just move the chip that matches the trans into the corrent ECM. <P>84 L4 ECM is the 6156. (correction)<BR>85-86 L4 ECM is the 6864.<BR>87/88 L4 ECM is the 7748.<BR>85 V6 ECM is the 6869.<BR>86-88 V6 ECM is the 7170.<P><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 02-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||02-07-2001||05:58 PM||||So everything is the same in an '85 GT auto and an '85 GT stick <I>except</I> the PROM?  I hope so 'cause I need to change ECMs (might help to figure out my electrical problems).||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||02-07-2001||06:56 PM||||Yes MM. they are the same ECM. If the lable is still on it you can check the part numbers to be sure. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Joe4x4||02-07-2001||09:45 PM||||ok ..so the ECM in the 84-4 cyl stick<BR>is 6156<BR>and the 86-4cyl auto is 6864.<P>So thats a no go...rats<P>So I guess I need a ECM out of a 85-86 4cyl.<BR>time to go to the junk yard.<P>Thanks for the help.<P>------------------<BR>Fiero got fire<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/exp.gif">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/animated_cat.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Joe4x4||02-09-2001||10:07 AM||||ok....I found a 86-cp 4cyl in my local <BR>junk yard , pulled out the ECM ( it was a stick ).<BR>Pulled out the ECM in my 86-cp, put the ECM <BR>( the one I got from the junk yard )<BR>in it with the PROM ( auto from my fiero ).<P>It fired right up, drove it around for few minites...than the check engine light came on.<BR> <BR>codes<P>1-2.....normal<BR>4-4.....lean exhaust<BR>5-1.....PROM<P>HELP<P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Joe4x4||02-09-2001||12:33 PM||||got it....I disconnected the battery.<BR>That took care of the PROM code.<BR>The code 44 ....I unpluged the o2 sensor and<BR>replugged it, and made sure no leaks .<P>No More ...check engine light  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Fiero got fire<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/exp.gif">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/animated_cat.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||terryk||02-09-2001||01:26 PM||||You're now an expert!||||reg||14
Z||000012||Joe4x4||02-09-2001||04:23 PM||||thanks ....TerryK<P>You helped me pick the right ECM out of the junk yard.||||reg||6
